Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: what the reading of the corrected question
 found

A third reader read the commit before this one alone, because the defect
it corrects was in code that no test reaches. The question takes its
answers now; what follows is what that reading found besides.

- A question that something else closed was taken for "stay". What closes
  every dialog (the visualisation window as it closes, Dialog.Close(all),
  a game that starts, a skin that is loaded again) leaves the dialog with
  "no" for its result, like a press of that button; the display was then
  not offered again, and the log said that the user had chosen. The yes/no
  dialog now tells a press of its "no" button (IsDeclined()), and only
  that, or going back, is "stay"; a dialog closed by something else was
  answered by nobody, and its display is offered again.
- A question that sat under another dialog (one opened over it, by an
  add-on for instance) ran out of time there, and came back only when the
  other dialog closed, perhaps minutes later, with the user at the screen:
  Kodi was then started again unasked. A question that comes back more
  than ten seconds after its time is not taken as left unanswered.
- Kodi is not started again unasked while a library is being updated or a
  recording runs or is about to, which is when Kodi does not turn the
  system off by itself either (CApplicationPowerHandling::CheckShutdown()).
- On no output, one look is owed at the start: a display that came between
  the last look of the start and the moment this began to listen was in
  neither. And the first look, where nothing is known yet, is not held up
  by what plays.
- Two displays plugged in together: when the best of them is settled and
  Kodi stays, the next best is offered at once. It was counted as seen,
  and never offered.
- What was kept of an offer is dropped when its looks are given up, and
  the wait starts anew for another display. Looks that fail are told in
  the log (three times), also where the devices cannot be listed, which
  nothing told.
- Setting the mode of the output keeps the watch from looking for a while,
  as setting up a video does.

What is decided is in DRMOutputChoice.h, for the host test: how what came
back from the question is read (ReadAnswer()), what is done when nobody
answered (WhenNobodyAnswers()), and how long after a look that failed the
next is taken. The test has 14 more checks for them.

Read and compiled, not run on a graphics device.
